  "description": "SAFHIT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H142 Ce4 Co4 O43 P12,0.5(C6 H14),4.25(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co7 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co8 (Co) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 10 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.591-3.757 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.24-114.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce4(LOEt)4O7H2] (C68H142Ce4Co4O43P12).",
